.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-LIST-SUBSCRIPTIONS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-list-subscriptions \- list the subscriptions of a bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm list-subscriptions
.BR \-\-bucket | \-b
.I BUCKET-ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists every subscription fanning out object-created notifications from a
bucket, identified by its Euclid resource name (ERN). Each subscription
is printed with its own ERN (usable with
.BR euclid-cli-esm-unsubscribe (1)),
its type, and its target ERN.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fIBUCKET-ERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the bucket whose subscriptions are listed.
Required.
.PP
The bucket may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The bucket's subscriptions are printed as JSON (an empty list if it has
none).
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, or the server could not be reached.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm list-subscriptions \e
    --bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:uploads
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-subscribe (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-unsubscribe (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
